.Dd November 27, 2026
.Dt unixts2time 1
.Os unixts2time
.\" ###### Name #############################################################
.Sh NAME
.Nm unixts2time
.Nd converts Unix timestamps to date/time strings
.\" ###### Synopsis #########################################################
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm unixts2time
.Op Fl T Ar time\_format\_template | Fl \-template Ar time\_format\_template
.br
.Op Fl H | Fl \-human\-readable
.br
.Op Fl s | Fl \-seconds
.br
.Op Fl m | Fl \-milliseconds
.br
.Op Fl u | Fl \-microseconds
.br
.Op Fl n | Fl \-nanoseconds
.br
.Op Ar unix\_timestamp ...
.Nm unixts2time
.Op Fl h | Fl \-help
.Nm unixts2time
.Op Fl v | Fl \-version
.\" ###### Description ######################################################
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm unixts2time
converts Unix timestamps to UTC date/time strings (by default in the format
.Ql %Y\-%m\-%d %H:%M:%S[.SSSSSSSSS] ,
with fractional digits scaled to the timestamp precision).
A Unix timestamp expresses the elapsed time in nanoseconds, microseconds,
milliseconds, or seconds relative to the Unix Epoch
(January 1, 1970, 00:00:00.000000000 UTC).
.Pp
By default, the timestamp granularity is auto\-detected from the integer part
using the following heuristic:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Seconds (s): from
0 (1970\-01\-01 00:00:00) to 4999999999 = 5e9\-1 (2128\-06\-11 08:53:19), and
\-4999999999 = \-(5e9\-1) (1811\-07\-23 15:06:41) to \-1 (1969\-12\-31 23:59:59);
.It
Milliseconds (ms): from
5000000000 = 5e9 (1970\-02\-27 20:53:20.000) to 4999999999999 = 5e12\-1 (2128\-06\-11 08:53:19.999), and
\-4999999999999 = \-(5e12\-1) (1811\-07\-23 15:06:40.001) to \-5000000000 = \-5e9 (1969\-11\-04 03:06:40.000);
.It
Microseconds (\[mc]s): from
5000000000000 = 5e12 (1970\-02\-27 20:53:20.000000) to 4999999999999999 = 5e15\-1 (2128\-06\-11 08:53:19.999999), and
\-4999999999999999 = \-(5e15\-1) (1811\-07\-23 15:06:40.000001) to \-5000000000000 = \-5e12 (1969\-11\-04 03:06:40.000000);
.It
Nanoseconds (ns):
5000000000000000 = 5e15 (1970\-02\-27 20:53:20.000000000) and above, and
\-5000000000000000 = \-5e15 (1969\-11\-04 03:06:40.000000000) and below.
.El
.Pp
Unless working with sub\-second timestamps very close to 1969/1970, the distant
past, or the distant future, auto\-detection selects the intended unit
automatically. Otherwise, the unit can be specified explicitly.
.\" ###### Arguments ########################################################
.Sh ARGUMENTS
The following arguments and options are available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Ar unix\_timestamp ...
One or more Unix timestamps to convert.
If no
.Ar unix\_timestamp
is provided, the current system time is used.
Timestamps may be given as integers or fixed\-point decimal numbers.
Integer values may use a
.Ql 0x
prefix for hexadecimal (base 16) or a leading
.Ql 0
for octal (base 8); otherwise decimal (base 10) is used.
.It Fl T Ar time\_format\_template | Fl \-template Ar time\_format\_template
Sets the template for formatting the date/time strings (default:
.Ql %Y\-%m\-%d %H:%M:%S )
according to
.Xr strftime 3 .
.It Fl H | Fl \-human\-readable
Include decimal, hexadecimal, and unit details in human\-readable form (default: off).
.It Fl s | Fl \-seconds
Interpret the input timestamp in seconds (default: auto\-detection).
.It Fl m | Fl \-milliseconds
Interpret the input timestamp in milliseconds (default: auto\-detection).
.It Fl u | Fl \-microseconds
Interpret the input timestamp in microseconds (default: auto\-detection).
.It Fl n | Fl \-nanoseconds
Interpret the input timestamp in nanoseconds (default: auto\-detection).
.It Fl h | Fl \-help
Prints the program's command\-line parameters and exits.
.It Fl v | Fl \-version
Prints the program version and exits.
.El
.\" ###### Exit status ######################################################
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
tool exits with 0 on success, and >0 in case of an error.
.\" ###### Examples #########################################################
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -bullet
.It
unixts2time
.It
unixts2time \-\-human\-readable
.It
unixts2time \-\-human\-readable \-\-seconds 1773744755
.It
unixts2time \-\-human\-readable \-\-seconds \-\- \-1000000
.It
unixts2time \-\-human\-readable \-\-milliseconds \-\- \-442460258000
.It
unixts2time \-\-seconds 1 1000 1000000 1000000000 2000000000
.It
unixts2time \-s 1773736279
.It
unixts2time \-\-milliseconds 212847000000
.It
unixts2time \-H 212847008123456789
.It
unixts2time 0x179cb2ae8af3dd89
.It
unixts2time \-H 0x179cb2ae8af3dd89
.It
unixts2time \-s 212847123.123
.It
unixts2time 1788550214.7787085
.It
unixts2time \-T \[dq]%x %X\[dq] \-n 2096218885000000000
.It
unixts2time \-T \[dq]%b %d %H:%M:%S %Y %Z\[dq] 1773736279
.It
unixts2time \-T \[dq]%b %d %H:%M:%S %Y %Z\[dq] 1784186916836355733
.It
unixts2time \-T \[dq]%x %X\[dq] 1784186916836355733
.It
unixts2time \-\-help
.It
unixts2time \-h
.It
unixts2time \-\-version
.It
unixts2time \-v
.El
